5. DEFECT FOUND AND FIXED
-------------------------
Add-RuntimeEnvironment.ps1 failed with "Cannot process argument because the value of argument
"name" is not valid" because its helper declared the parameter as $PropName while every call site
passed -Name. Windows PowerShell 5.1 silently accepted the unmatched named argument, left the
parameter null and failed later inside the property lookup. Fixed by renaming the parameter to
$Name in the helper, re-parsed the script, re-ran the functional self-test (all green), and
redeployed the fixed file to D:\program_runtime_environment\tools\ (hash verified).

6. FOLLOW-UP NOTES
------------------
- The D: write path needs danger-full-access approval each time; expect one approval prompt per
  runtime environment installation. This is expected and documented.
- python on PATH resolves to the Microsoft Store alias stub, which is not a real interpreter;
  the first real Python need should install python into D:\program_runtime_environment\python.
- To change the standard: edit policy\storage-policy.json and policy\output-storage-policy.md,
  mirror policy\deploy\global-agents.md, then run tools\Install-GlobalPolicy.ps1.
- To extend the standard to another workspace:
  tools\Install-GlobalPolicy.ps1 -TargetWorkspace <path>.